# JetonBro .cursorrules

## Scope
- No card or dice simulation, ever. No hand evaluation, ever. Physical cards
  and dice are played by humans, offline. If a task seems to require the app
  to understand cards, dice, or hand rankings, stop and flag it — do not
  implement it, even as a helper or shortcut.
- Manual hand-entry/photo fields (per jetonbro-requirements-v4.md) are
  display-only. Never parse, OCR, or score them.
- No real money, no real-money rails, no payment integrations.
- No poker side-pot math (uneven all-ins) in v1 — single pot only.

## Architecture
- Protocol-specific logic (blackjack/poker/zilch) lives only in its protocol
  config object (actions, phases, roles, payout rule) as defined in
  jetonbro-requirements-v4.md. Never as bespoke branching code per game.
  Adding a new game means adding a new config object, not new code paths.
- Exactly one service module mutates wallet or escrow-ledger rows. No other
  file writes to a wallet or ledger row, directly or indirectly.
- The personal ledger (Standings) is a derived read-model over existing
  RELEASE events. It is never written to independently, except for the
  explicit "Clear" action, which itself must write its own manual-settlement
  ledger entry rather than deleting history.
- Every REST route, socket event, and app-defined action type must be
  registered in docs/ROUTE_MANIFEST.md in the same PR that introduces it.
  Before adding any of the three, check the manifest for an existing
  equivalent — extend it, don't duplicate it.

## Hygiene
- No dead code, no commented-out routes, no unused wrapper functions in a
  merged PR — delete or don't merge.
- Every new-file PR states which existing module it extends, or confirms
  this is genuinely new functionality with no existing overlap.
- Keep the frontend sharp and the backend minimal — if a proposed backend
  addition doesn't map to something explicit in jetonbro-requirements-v4.md,
  flag it before building it rather than building it speculatively.
